    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "B.F. Robertson platted Foley in 1879, and the town officially incorporated in May 1900 with its first Board of Trustees.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21,
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityoffoleymo.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A post office has served Foley continuously since 1880, marking the town’s early communication hub.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Foley%2C_Missouri"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Foley sits just 1.5 miles from the Mississippi River and 51 miles north of St. Louis, offering a quiet riverside feel.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
